WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.969
JAMIE: What does "climbed too far"
actually mean, though? That phrase gets
used

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:05.938
JAMIE: every time anything goes up.

00:00:06.048 --> 00:00:10.540
RUFUS: Fair. What it means in practice
is that enough investors decided the

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:15.031
RUFUS: previous day's gain wasn't
supported by new evidence of actual
value —

00:00:15.031 --> 00:00:19.523
RUFUS: earnings, products, contracts —
and started selling. Yesterday's price
move was the

00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:24.015
RUFUS: belief. Today's reversal was the
doubt. That's what AP is describing.

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:27.829
JAMIE: Okay, but here's what I keep
coming back to. When the Nasdaq

00:00:27.829 --> 00:00:31.533
JAMIE: drops 1.5% because "AI stocks
reversed," people with index funds just
had

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:35.236
JAMIE: a bad day and they probably don't
know why. They didn't make

00:00:35.236 --> 00:00:38.940
JAMIE: a bet on AI valuations.
